    {
      "title": "top_category finds the highest total and breaks ties alphabetically",
      "description": "Create top_category(transactions, kind) in expense_manager/top_category.py. Each transaction uses the standard record shape. Use category_totals from expense_manager/category_totals.py (already written, shown below). If multiple categories have equal totals, return the alphabetically first category. Raise ValueError when there are no matching records.\n1. totals = category_totals(transactions, kind)\n2. if len(totals) == 0: raise ValueError\n3. best = None\n4. For each category in sorted(totals):\n   - if best is None or totals[category] > totals[best]: best = category\n5. return best\n",
      "commit": "feat: find top transaction category",
      "tests": [
        "tests/test_top_category.py"
